Your C draft had three defects: XACE callback returns void not int; XACE_READ/WRITE/DESTROY are nonexistent; masking access can bypass denial. Corrected primary proposal below uses unconditional denial on foreign owner and preserves privilege logic and existing init failure handling. Verify and propose corrections ONLY if concrete defects remain. Full Selection definition from dix/selection_priv.h includes ClientPtr client. XaceSelectionAccessRec has Selection **ppSel; pinned dixLookupSelection always passes &pSel. Limit 180 words.
#include "dix/selection_priv.h"
static void selection_access(CallbackListPtr *list, void *unused, void *data)
{
    XaceSelectionAccessRec *rec = data;
    (void)list; (void)unused;
    if (SpatialSecurityPrivileged(rec->client)) return;
    Selection *selection = *rec->ppSel;
    if (selection && selection->client &&
        !SpatialSecuritySameApplication(rec->client, selection->client))
        rec->status = BadAccess;
}
// Init: add !XaceRegisterCallback(XACE_SELECTION_ACCESS, selection_access, NULL) to existing OR chain.
